# Stage lighting
@scenario tutorial_lesson_24
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Compare the sprite and background under the default lighting and the {b}dusk{/b} preset. Start by looking at the face and the edge of the sleeve.
# region apply_dusk
[stage dusk]
# endregion
[if !tutorial_still]
[move ginger rightmark ease_in_out_cubic 640]
[wait 640]
[move ginger rightmark thoughtful exprdur=90]
[endif]
ginger: The dusk preset is active. Check which parts of the sprite are lit and how well its outline separates from the background.
[stage clear]
[if !tutorial_still]
[move ginger guide ease_out_cubic 510]
[wait 510]
[move ginger guide normal exprdur=90]
[endif]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/24_layer_groups_and_lighting.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt apply_dusk]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: That single command applied the preset. The original lighting is back after [stage clear]. Both views use the same sprite art.
[set tutorial_source scripts/definitions/dusk.stagepreset]
[set tutorial_excerpt exposure]
ginger: Open scripts/definitions/dusk.stagepreset in Lighting Studio. Adjust exposure, save and replay. Compare the two lighting states again at the same window size.
ginger: A stage preset has several independent settings. Exposure changes the background's overall brightness. Tint also has a colour, a strength and a blend mode. The preset file records those separately.
ginger: Pick a neutral part of the background and an edge of the character. Use the same two points in both captures so your comparison is repeatable.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Compare the preset with a control -> practice
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: Which command restores the default lighting?
> Hide Ginger. -> retry
> Use the stage clear command. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: Hiding the character would remove the sprite while leaving the preset active on the stage.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Use [stage clear]. The next line then renders without the dusk preset.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_24]
[flag tutorial_done_24]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_3]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/definitions/dusk.stagepreset]
[set tutorial_excerpt exposure]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Start with the cleared stage and capture the room. Apply dusk and capture the same settled pose. Keep the change of pose or position out of your brightness comparison.
ginger: In Lighting Studio change only background exposure. Replay dusk and compare the neutral patch with your first dusk capture. Keep the tint settings at their original values.
ginger: Restore exposure, then change tint strength with the same tint colour and blend mode. Inspect the background and the outline separately before deciding which setting caused a difference.
ginger: Finally return to the default state. If later dialogue still uses dusk, trace the path to the stage clear command, including any jump that can bypass it.
@label practice_question
ginger: You want to measure just the contribution of tint strength. Which pair of captures does that?
> Default and dusk with several settings changed. -> practice_hint
> Two dusk captures with only tint strength changed. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: Changing several inputs at once shows the combined result. Keep exposure, colour, blend mode and framing fixed for this comparison.
[jump practice_question]
@label practice_result
ginger: The first pair holds the other preset inputs fixed. Check the same background patch in both images and record the original and changed strength.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the exercise again -> practice
> Back to topics -> return_hub
